Sure! Here’s how you’d invoke the `emitNewLineBeforeLeadingComments` helper so that it inserts a newline before the leading comments of the node at position 42:

```js
// Assuming `tsLineMap` and `tsWriter` are already defined elsewhere in your code:
functions.emitNewLineBeforeLeadingComments({
  lineMap: tsLineMap,   // the line‑map object for the TS source
  writer: tsWriter,     // the writer instance that emits text into the file
  node: 42              // the numeric position of the node you’re targeting
  // leadingComments defaults to an empty array if omitted
});
```

That call tells the helper to look up the line information from `tsLineMap`, write the appropriate newline via `tsWriter`, and apply it right before the leading comments of the node located at offset 42. If you have a specific set of leading comments you want to handle, you can also supply them explicitly via the optional `leadingComments` property.
